CORE
unpacked_struct_array1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.c\.p_in\] always main\.c\.i\[1\] == 22'h7FF: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.c2\.p_in\] always main\.c2\.i\[1\] == 22'h7FF: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.x\[0\]\.b == 42 && main\.x\[0\]\.a == 0\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always \(##1 main\.x\[1\]\.a == 3 && main\.x\[1\]\.b == 5\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p2\] always \(##1 main\.m\[0\]\[1\]\.b == 5\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p3\] always main\.z\[1\] == 22'h7FF: PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Unpacked arrays of a packed struct and of a packed vector of the same width
are equivalent types (1800-2017 6.22.2), and may be connected to each other.
